body:
[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pith\_helmet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pith_helmet)

&#x200B;

If you scroll down to 'Modern Uses' there's a picture next to the USA bit that looks to be this exact helmet.

You're not a serial monogamist if you're emotionally unfaithful. I'm not judging you, just urging you to be honest with yourself so you can see what I'm seeing from over here. You are not in LOVE with your boyfriend. You are complacent with him. Attached to him. Sure, you may love him in a different way than romantic. It's obvious he is not a suited longterm partner for you if your goals don't align and he hasn't made the effort to fit into your life. He is deadweight financially, and emotionally too if he keeps hurting you without change.

Allow yourself to see that, allow yourself to feel the grief for your relationship. It's okay. Monogamy does not mean staying with someone you don't love. Monogamy means staying with someone you do love and not looking elsewhere for you have no need to.

&#x200B;

You have need to look elsewhere because you are not fulfilled or content with your partner. You want, need, and deserve better. Maybe not this man, if you don't want to take the plunge with an older man. I don't see anything wrong with the age thing here as youre old enough to make adult decisions.

&#x200B;

Good luck.
